      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start, thanks. It's pretty concise, which is good, but I'm worried it's a bit too brief for a full study guide. \n\nCould you expand on it? Try to go into more detail about the specific phases (prophase, metaphase, anaphase, telophase) so students really get the mechanics. \n\nAlso, just a reminder—the ranking tool is going to flag this if the score is too low. So while I definitely don't want you to just spam the words, try to make sure use of those \"pedagogical\" words is sufficient so the draft actually gets seen by the reviewers. Just keep it natural!",
